Chapter: DnsAnswerCount
  cites Net chapter DnsResolver
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 We say:

Section: Fixtures

 A DNS header and nothing after it. qdcount 0, so the answer walk starts at 12
 and stops immediately because off + 10 passes the end of a 12-byte datagram.
 ancount is what the wire CLAIMS, and it is the only thing that differs between
 the two arms.

  hdr : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  hdr (qd) (an) =
    [18, 52, 129, 128]
    & [bit-and (bit-shru qd 8) 255, bit-and qd 255]
    & [bit-and (bit-shru an 8) 255, bit-and an 255]
    & [0, 0, 0, 0]

  honest : List Integer = hdr 0 0
  lying : List Integer = hdr 0 100

  name-of : Maybe (List Integer) -> Text
  name-of (m) = when m
    is Just (ip) -> "just-" & show (list-length ip)
    is None -> "none"

Section: The Arms

 honest is the positive control. A parser that refused everything, or one that
 answered none to every question, would pass the lying arm on its own.

  h : DnsResponse = dns-parse-response honest
  l : DnsResponse = dns-parse-response lying

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("honest-valid=" & show (h.valid))
    print-line-uni ("honest-count=" & show (h.answer-count))
    print-line-uni ("honest-lookup=" & name-of (dns-first-a-record h))
    print-line-uni ("honest-ttl=" & show (dns-first-a-ttl h))
    print-line-uni ("lying-valid=" & show (l.valid))
    print-line-uni ("lying-count=" & show (l.answer-count))
    print-line-uni ("count-matches-list=" & show (l.answer-count == list-length (l.answers)))
    print-line-uni ("lying-lookup=" & name-of (dns-first-a-record l))
    print-line-uni ("lying-ttl=" & show (dns-first-a-ttl l))
    print-line-uni ("survived")
  end
